{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C++ header file", "description": "This file defines a set of template classes and utility structures for managing proxy objects, reference counting, object pools, and container types within the WPEFramework Core namespace. It includes implementations for proxy objects with custom allocators, lists, queues, and maps for managing these proxy objects, as well as mechanisms for linking, notification, and lifecycle management of objects, mainly used for modular and thread-safe resource management in the framework.", "external_files": ["<memory>", "<atomic>", "Portability.h", "StateTrigger.h", "Sync.h", "TypeTraits.h"], "external_methods": ["::malloc", "::free", "::SleepMs", "memcmp", "memmove", "memset", "memcpy", "ASSERT", "TRACE_L1", "TRACE_L5", "Core::InterlockedIncrement", "Core::Inifinite", "Core::ERROR_NONE", "Core::ERROR_DESTRUCTION_SUCCEEDED"], "published": ["ProxyObject", "ProxyType", "ProxyList", "ProxyQueue", "UnlinkStorage", "ProxyContainerType", "ProxyMapType", "ProxyPoolType"], "classes": [{"name": "ProxyObject", "description": "A final template class that wraps a context object, providing thread-safe reference counting, custom memory management, and lifecycle control. It prevents assignment for reference counted objects and offers methods for store, clear, size, and managing object dependencies."}, {"name": "ProxyType", "description": "A helper class managing pointers to context objects, including creation, reference counting, casting operators, and object lifecycle management. It supports dynamic casting and inheritance hierarchies for proxy objects."}, {"name": "ProxyList", "description": "A template class implementing a fast, non-thread-safe list of IReferenceCounted pointers with dynamic resizing capability. It supports add, remove, find, clear, and iteration operations."}, {"name": "ProxyQueue", "description": "A queue class enforcing a producer-consumer pattern for proxy objects with thread synchronization, allowin